 # 3D Perlin-like Noise and Fractal Brownian Motion (FBM)
 
-Also called: 3D Perlin Noise, 3D Perlin-like Noise, 3D Worley-Perlin Fractal Erosion Noise, Cloud Noise, FBM Cloud Density, Fractal Brownian Motion, Fractional Brownian Motion, fBm
+Also called: Fractal Brownian Motion, Fractional Brownian Motion, 3D Perlin Noise, 3D Perlin-like Noise
 
 ## Overview
-3D Perlin-like Noise generates smooth pseudo-random scalar values on a 3D unit lattice using hash-derived gradient vectors, Hermite smoothing, and trilinear interpolation [S1, S2, unofficial][S4, unofficial][S10, unofficial]. Fractal Brownian Motion (FBM) constructs multi-scale fractal noise by summing multiple octaves of a base noise function (such as Perlin noise) with scaled frequency and amplitude [S3][S4, unofficial][S5, unofficial]. Together, they solve the problem of generating natural-looking volumetric textures (e.g., clouds, terrain, smoke) that lack the repetitive, uniform appearance of single-layer noise [S3][S4, unofficial]. They differ from [Simplex Noise](978-simplex-noise.md) by using a cubic lattice with trilinear interpolation rather than a simplex grid with tetrahedral interpolation, and from [Improved Perlin Noise (4D)](3723-improved-perlin-noise-4d.md) by operating in 3D space with standard cubic smoothing functions [S1, S2, unofficial][S10, unofficial].
+3D Perlin-like Noise generates smooth pseudo-random scalar values on a 3D unit lattice using hash-derived corner values, Hermite smoothing, and trilinear interpolation [S1, S2, unofficial][S4, unofficial]. Fractal Brownian Motion (FBM) constructs multi-scale fractal noise by summing multiple octaves of a base noise function with scaled frequency and amplitude [S3][S4, unofficial][S5, unofficial]. Together, they solve the problem of generating natural-looking volumetric textures (e.g., clouds, terrain, smoke) that lack the repetitive, uniform appearance of single-layer noise [S3][S4, unofficial]. They differ from [Simplex Noise](978-simplex-noise.md) by using a cubic lattice with trilinear interpolation rather than a simplex grid with tetrahedral interpolation, and from [Improved Perlin Noise (4D)](3723-improved-perlin-noise-4d.md) by operating in 3D space with standard cubic smoothing functions [S1, S2, unofficial][S10, unofficial].
 
